  "query_preview": "..A ridge centered over the Four Corners will keep dry \nand seasonably warm weather in place through at least early next \nweek. Surface high pressure over the central plains will maintain \nour locally gusty easterly winds, especially today. Wind gusts could \nreach 30 mph at times over higher terrain.\n\nBy Tuesday and Wednesday, the ridge begins to break down as a weak \ntrough attempts to form over western Arizona. This will allow the \natmosphere to destabilize just enough to introduce a high-based \nconvective threat for Wednesday.  \n\nThe ridge then briefly rebuilds later next week, before possibly \nbreaking down again next weekend. It is next weekend or early the \nfollowing week that may bring more significant weather to our area. \nThis pattern bears watching, but it is just outside the forecast \nperiod for now.",
